1
00:00:04,132 --> 00:00:05,841
(blood sloshing)

2
00:00:05,924 --> 00:00:07,882
(blood sizzles)

3
00:00:07,966 --> 00:00:10,340
Oh, that blood,
don't touch that.

4
00:00:10,424 --> 00:00:11,882
You think, I don't know that?

5
00:00:11,966 --> 00:00:13,340
(blood whooshes)
(Kugisaki gasps)

6
00:00:14,925 --> 00:00:19,216
Now run away with
your backs to me.

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,300
(ground rumbling)

8
00:00:20,383 --> 00:00:23,508
-(Itadori grunting)
-(streams of blood crashing)

9
00:00:23,591 --> 00:00:26,133
Come on Kugisaki, is that
the fastest you can run?

10
00:00:26,216 --> 00:00:27,508
Oh, shut up!

11
00:00:27,591 --> 00:00:28,842
(streams of blood sloshing)

12
00:00:28,925 --> 00:00:31,675
-(Kugisaki grunts)
-(Kugisaki thuds)

13
00:00:31,758 --> 00:00:34,717
-(Itadori grunts)
-(stream of blood crashing)

14
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,800
I've got your back.

15
00:00:36,758 --> 00:00:37,174
Oh, great.

16
00:00:37,258 --> 00:00:40,091
(ground thuds)

17
00:00:40,174 --> 00:00:41,550
Huh?

18
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:44,551
(ground thundering)

19
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:47,884
(Kugisaki groans)

20
00:00:47,968 --> 00:00:49,718
What amazing speed,

21
00:00:49,801 --> 00:00:52,010
and while carrying someone too.

22
00:00:52,092 --> 00:00:56,175
(streams of blood gushing)

23
00:00:56,259 --> 00:00:57,884
They're getting away.

24
00:00:57,968 --> 00:00:59,592
Well, no matter.

25
00:01:01,426 --> 00:01:03,759
(Itadori grunts)

26
00:01:03,843 --> 00:01:07,010
(Itadori whooshes)

27
00:01:07,092 --> 00:01:08,010
(Itadori and Kugisaki thud)

28
00:01:08,092 --> 00:01:09,968
(Itadori and Kugisaki grunt)

29
00:01:12,426 --> 00:01:14,176
Okay, we're out of his range.

30
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:17,427
[Kugisaki] Well done.

31
00:01:17,510 --> 00:01:18,343
I'll make sure you get a medal.

32
00:01:18,427 --> 00:01:20,510
[Itadori] Yeah, yeah.

33
00:01:20,593 --> 00:01:22,385
[Kugisaki] I'm
kidding, thank you.

34
00:01:22,468 --> 00:01:23,468
(Itadori gasps)

35
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:24,760
(Itadori grunts)

36
00:01:24,844 --> 00:01:26,385
-(blood gushing)
-(Kechizu gurgling)

37
00:01:26,468 --> 00:01:29,760
(blood swooshing)

38
00:01:29,844 --> 00:01:32,593
I guess it took a shortcut
and got here ahead of us.

39
00:01:32,677 --> 00:01:37,635
-Itadori!
-(blood smashes)

40
00:01:38,635 --> 00:01:40,427
(Kugisaki groans)

41
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:41,760
[Itadori] Kugisaki!

42
00:01:41,844 --> 00:01:44,136
You don't need to worry
about that too much.

43
00:01:44,219 --> 00:01:45,428
My younger brother's blood

44
00:01:45,511 --> 00:01:47,219
doesn't have the
same quality as mine

45
00:01:47,303 --> 00:01:50,594
and even mine probably
won't kill you outright,

46
00:01:50,678 --> 00:01:54,761
unless you manage to get
your entire body bathed in it.

47
00:01:54,845 --> 00:01:58,053
Though, I can assure
you it will hurt like hell.

48
00:01:58,136 --> 00:01:59,219
Now we've reached the time

49
00:01:59,303 --> 00:02:02,053
where our technique
actually begins.

50
00:02:02,136 --> 00:02:04,428
Rot Technique! Decay!

51
00:02:05,720 --> 00:02:08,594
(flesh squelching)

52
00:02:11,678 --> 00:02:13,013
[Kugisaki] Huh?

53
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:23,220
-(Opening theme music)
-(singing in Japanese)

54
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:46,682
My blood, like
that of my brothers

55
00:03:46,765 --> 00:03:47,515
is absorbed by the victims,

56
00:03:47,598 --> 00:03:50,557
through their wounds
and membranes.

57
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:53,265
And then once any of us
brothers activate the technique

58
00:03:53,348 --> 00:03:55,390
it quickly begins
to rot you away

59
00:03:55,473 --> 00:03:58,265
from the point of incursion.

60
00:03:58,348 --> 00:04:01,473
I'd give that young
man about 15 minutes.

61
00:04:01,557 --> 00:04:03,348
10 minutes, max,
for you, young lady.

62
00:04:05,432 --> 00:04:09,098
By morning, nothing
but bones will remain.

63
00:04:09,181 --> 00:04:10,725
If it's a technique,

64
00:04:10,808 --> 00:04:12,599
we just need to
make them release it.

65
00:04:13,641 --> 00:04:15,725
So, then it is toxic.

66
00:04:15,808 --> 00:04:18,391
The end result is
essentially that of a poison,

67
00:04:18,474 --> 00:04:19,975
but, I assure you our technique

68
00:04:20,058 --> 00:04:22,766
is purely one of decomposition.

69
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:24,492
Now that I finished
revealing our technique

70
00:04:24,516 --> 00:04:28,308
they'll actually end
up dying even faster.

71
00:04:28,391 --> 00:04:31,224
So, what will you do now?

72
00:04:32,474 --> 00:04:36,599
Elder brother, these sorcerers
didn't amount to much.

73
00:04:36,683 --> 00:04:38,099
[Narrator] During the Meiji era,

74
00:04:38,182 --> 00:04:39,599
there was a girl
with a unique trait

75
00:04:39,683 --> 00:04:42,600
that allowed her to bear
a cursed spirit's child.

76
00:04:42,684 --> 00:04:44,767
She conceived a child
without knowing how

77
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:46,600
and the criticism she endured

78
00:04:46,684 --> 00:04:48,434
from her parents and
relatives was extreme.

79
00:04:48,517 --> 00:04:51,142
She fled with her baby's corpse,

80
00:04:51,225 --> 00:04:54,517
ending up at a temple run
by a certain jujutsu sorcerer.

81
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,660
That's where her luck ran out.

82
00:04:55,684 --> 00:04:57,517
(blood splats)

83
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,267
Noritoshi Kamo.

84
00:04:59,350 --> 00:05:00,976
In jujutsu sorcery's legacy,

85
00:05:01,059 --> 00:05:03,767
he's remembered as
the most vile of sorcerers.

86
00:05:03,851 --> 00:05:06,183
A disgrace to the
three major clans.

87
00:05:06,267 --> 00:05:08,267
He was captivated
by the possibility

88
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:11,810
of a child born of a
human and a cursed spirit.

89
00:05:11,893 --> 00:05:14,268
Nine times he impregnated her.

90
00:05:14,351 --> 00:05:15,435
Nine times he aborted her.

91
00:05:15,518 --> 00:05:18,019
All records of how he did it

92
00:05:18,101 --> 00:05:20,601
and what happened to her
afterward, were destroyed.

93
00:05:20,685 --> 00:05:22,661
The Cursed Wombs Death
Paintings, one through three,

94
00:05:22,685 --> 00:05:25,435
became cursed objects
powerful enough

95
00:05:25,518 --> 00:05:27,810
to be classified
as special-grade.

96
00:05:27,893 --> 00:05:29,435
Perhaps the origin of that power

97
00:05:29,518 --> 00:05:33,019
was the mother's
resentment, or perhaps...

98
00:05:33,143 --> 00:05:35,685
[Eso] I have no
memories of a mother.

99
00:05:35,768 --> 00:05:37,852
Humans, sorcerers.

100
00:05:37,935 --> 00:05:40,894
It's not that I hold any
special grudge against them.

101
00:05:42,144 --> 00:05:44,644
For 150 years, we've
remained sealed away

102
00:05:44,728 --> 00:05:48,394
with nothing but each
other's existence to rely on.

103
00:05:48,477 --> 00:05:50,853
We'll side with
the cursed spirits.

104
00:05:50,936 --> 00:05:51,728
Are you sure about that?

105
00:05:51,811 --> 00:05:54,686
They seemed shady
to me, elder brother.

106
00:05:55,936 --> 00:05:57,561
The future those
cursed spirits painted

107
00:05:57,644 --> 00:05:59,020
is more convenient for us.

108
00:05:59,102 --> 00:06:00,853
That's all there is to it.

109
00:06:00,936 --> 00:06:02,394
You can forget about owing them

110
00:06:02,477 --> 00:06:05,644
for our current manifestation.

111
00:06:05,728 --> 00:06:06,808
And now listen up brothers.

112
00:06:07,728 --> 00:06:10,603
Eso, you live for Kechizu.

113
00:06:10,687 --> 00:06:13,103
Kechizu, you live for me.

114
00:06:13,186 --> 00:06:14,645
And I'll live for you, Eso.

115
00:06:14,729 --> 00:06:17,603
We three are one.

116
00:06:17,687 --> 00:06:19,145
I live for my brothers.

117
00:06:20,186 --> 00:06:22,228
If it is what my brothers desire

118
00:06:22,312 --> 00:06:25,437
I will gladly give my life
to grant that wish for them.

119
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:27,930
If the suffering is too great

120
00:06:27,979 --> 00:06:31,895
would you like me to end
you right away as a merciful act?

121
00:06:31,979 --> 00:06:33,021
(Kugisaki laughs)

122
00:06:33,103 --> 00:06:36,062
A technique that
guarantees victory once it hits.

123
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:37,520
You two are strong.

124
00:06:37,603 --> 00:06:38,688
You're screwed though,

125
00:06:38,771 --> 00:06:42,688
'cause that makes me the
worst possible match for you.

126
00:06:42,771 --> 00:06:43,688
(blue flame whooshes)

127
00:06:43,771 --> 00:06:44,438
Straw Doll Technique!

128
00:06:44,521 --> 00:06:47,063
-(nail clangs)
-Resonance!

129
00:06:47,146 --> 00:06:48,730
(Eso gags)

130
00:06:48,813 --> 00:06:50,438
(blood patters)

131
00:06:50,521 --> 00:06:53,229
Let's play a game of chicken.

132
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:56,146
You don't like pain
very much, do you?

133
00:06:56,229 --> 00:06:59,563
Then you'd better start crying
and release your technique!

134
00:06:59,646 --> 00:07:01,271
(Kechizu moans)

135
00:07:01,354 --> 00:07:04,104
[Eso] A technique that turns
the curse back on the user.

136
00:07:04,187 --> 00:07:05,771
It is a game of chicken.

137
00:07:05,855 --> 00:07:07,647
So unless I release
our technique,

138
00:07:07,731 --> 00:07:08,731
this pain will continue?

139
00:07:10,647 --> 00:07:13,105
[Kugisaki] Straw Doll
Technique, Resonance.

140
00:07:13,188 --> 00:07:14,731
It's a technique
that deals damage

141
00:07:14,814 --> 00:07:17,689
to the target's main body
by driving cursed energy

142
00:07:17,772 --> 00:07:19,772
through an effigy and a
lost portion of the target.

143
00:07:22,023 --> 00:07:25,314
The technique's range is
broad and the effect varies

144
00:07:25,397 --> 00:07:26,272
with the difference in strength

145
00:07:26,355 --> 00:07:28,897
between us and the
value of the lost portion.

146
00:07:30,355 --> 00:07:32,772
As far as Straw Doll
Technique is concerned,

147
00:07:32,856 --> 00:07:35,314
blood isn't very valuable.

148
00:07:35,397 --> 00:07:39,024
But, Resonance uses it
as the link to its target

149
00:07:39,732 --> 00:07:42,648
and the blood from both
of them that's inside me now

150
00:07:42,732 --> 00:07:46,565
is strongly linking us and
they're Rot Technique together.

151
00:07:48,273 --> 00:07:49,189
It's a nice surprise

152
00:07:49,273 --> 00:07:51,815
that it worked on the
younger brother, too.

153
00:07:51,898 --> 00:07:54,148
If I'm going to die here anyway

154
00:07:54,231 --> 00:07:57,523
then I'll just keep on
hammering Resonance into them.

155
00:07:57,606 --> 00:07:59,690
Yes, that pain is quite intense,

156
00:07:59,773 --> 00:08:00,833
but no matter how
many times she does it,

157
00:08:00,857 --> 00:08:02,648
it won't end our lives.

158
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:06,607
So, as long as we hold
out, you'll be the ones to die.

159
00:08:06,691 --> 00:08:09,816
Not to mention,
while Decay is active

160
00:08:09,899 --> 00:08:12,607
the pain and poison will
keep you from moving.

161
00:08:12,691 --> 00:08:14,983
(energy thunders)

162
00:08:15,066 --> 00:08:16,066
(Kechizu growls)

163
00:08:17,774 --> 00:08:19,524
[Eso] How were you
able to move that well?

164
00:08:19,607 --> 00:08:20,607
(Eso grunts)

165
00:08:20,649 --> 00:08:21,649
(Kechizu growls)

166
00:08:21,691 --> 00:08:23,858
(nail clangs)
[Kugisaki] Resonance!

167
00:08:25,899 --> 00:08:28,441
(punch thuds)

168
00:08:29,941 --> 00:08:31,691
Itadori is the vessel
for Ryomen Sukuna,

169
00:08:31,774 --> 00:08:35,482
the King of Curses
and Deadly Poisons.

170
00:08:35,566 --> 00:08:38,275
So, he has resistance
to all forms of poison.

171
00:08:38,358 --> 00:08:40,817
[Eso] The end result is
essentially that of a poison

172
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,483
but I assure you, our technique

173
00:08:42,567 --> 00:08:45,026
is purely one of decomposition.

174
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:46,543
[Kugisaki] He's
probably feeling pain

175
00:08:46,567 --> 00:08:47,734
from the decomposition

176
00:08:47,817 --> 00:08:49,692
but the resulting
poison doesn't affect him

177
00:08:49,775 --> 00:08:52,817
and if it's just pain...

178
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:55,026
(Itadori grunts)

179
00:08:55,108 --> 00:08:57,483
(Itadori thuds)

180
00:08:57,567 --> 00:08:59,026
Yuji Itadori!

181
00:08:59,108 --> 00:09:00,692
(Itadori grunting)

182
00:09:00,775 --> 00:09:02,775
Will never stop!

183
00:09:02,859 --> 00:09:07,234
-(Itadori grunting)
-(Kechizu groans)

184
00:09:07,318 --> 00:09:09,234
Kechizu!

185
00:09:09,318 --> 00:09:10,234
(nails clang)

186
00:09:10,318 --> 00:09:11,901
Just shut your mouth, huh?

187
00:09:12,609 --> 00:09:13,526
Resonance!

188
00:09:13,609 --> 00:09:14,609
It's nothing!

189
00:09:14,693 --> 00:09:17,693
(energy thundering)

190
00:09:17,776 --> 00:09:19,526
He switched.

191
00:09:19,609 --> 00:09:20,901
The woman was close to death

192
00:09:20,985 --> 00:09:23,860
so he matched her against
my brother who's also dying.

193
00:09:23,943 --> 00:09:27,234
Does she think she can
stop my movement forever?

194
00:09:27,318 --> 00:09:28,318
Damn you!

195
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:31,776
Do I released the
technique or not?

196
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,401
I can't go and save
my brother like this.

197
00:09:34,484 --> 00:09:36,736
I can't unleash Wing
King while Decay is active.

198
00:09:36,819 --> 00:09:40,069
But, does that woman
have enough strength left

199
00:09:40,152 --> 00:09:41,319
to kill my brother?

200
00:09:42,694 --> 00:09:44,652
Even with all of
her interference,

201
00:09:44,736 --> 00:09:48,902
this man won't be able
to kill me before she dies.

202
00:09:49,861 --> 00:09:53,069
So, I cannot release
the technique!

203
00:09:53,902 --> 00:09:55,610
(Kechizu gasping)

204
00:09:55,694 --> 00:09:56,569
(Kechizu yells)

205
00:09:56,652 --> 00:09:57,736
(Eso sobs)

206
00:09:57,819 --> 00:09:59,069
[Choso] We three are one.

207
00:09:59,152 --> 00:10:00,902
[Eso] I live for my brothers.

208
00:10:00,986 --> 00:10:03,277
(rock music)

209
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:08,320
-(Itadori and Eso grunting)
-(energy thundering)

210
00:10:12,153 --> 00:10:14,737
I was already releasing
it before I even knew it.

211
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:17,820
(punches thudding)

212
00:10:17,903 --> 00:10:19,320
Wing King!

213
00:10:19,403 --> 00:10:24,361
-(streams of blood swooshing)
-(rock music)

214
00:10:31,945 --> 00:10:33,695
(Kechizu growling)

215
00:10:33,778 --> 00:10:37,988
(nail clangs)

216
00:10:38,071 --> 00:10:39,863
(Itadori thuds)

217
00:10:39,946 --> 00:10:40,946
(blue light swooshes)

218
00:10:42,446 --> 00:10:43,904
(Kechizu roars)

219
00:10:43,988 --> 00:10:48,904
-(blue light swooshes)
-(rock music)

220
00:10:52,654 --> 00:10:55,696
(Kugisaki and Itadori grunt)

221
00:10:55,779 --> 00:10:58,321
♪ It's not right or wrong ♪

222
00:10:58,404 --> 00:11:00,988
-(blood gushes)
-(Kechizu roars)

223
00:11:01,071 --> 00:11:03,905
What? What was that
black light I saw just now?

224
00:11:04,864 --> 00:11:08,363
I know I reinforced my
arm with cursed energy

225
00:11:08,447 --> 00:11:10,363
just before taking his punch,

226
00:11:10,447 --> 00:11:12,031
and the next thing I knew,

227
00:11:12,113 --> 00:11:13,913
my whole arm and shoulder
had been blown away.

228
00:11:15,905 --> 00:11:19,822
(gasps) Younger brother,
please, don't you die.

229
00:11:20,947 --> 00:11:24,196
Elder brother!

230
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:25,280
(Itadori grunts)

231
00:11:27,655 --> 00:11:29,989
All right, I haven't shown
you this one yet, have I?

232
00:11:30,072 --> 00:11:32,530
(fingers snap)

233
00:11:32,613 --> 00:11:35,364
(nail sizzles)

234
00:11:36,448 --> 00:11:37,448
Hairpin.

235
00:11:39,823 --> 00:11:43,197
(Kechizu thuds)

236
00:11:43,281 --> 00:11:44,281
Don't worry.

237
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:48,032
I'll soon send your
older brother to join ya.

238
00:11:50,032 --> 00:11:51,032
Kechizu.

239
00:11:51,948 --> 00:11:52,865
[Choso] We three are one.

240
00:11:52,948 --> 00:11:55,865
[Eso] I'm sorry, elder brother.

241
00:11:57,489 --> 00:11:58,323
(Itadori gasps)

242
00:11:58,406 --> 00:12:01,781
Even though I was
with him, I... (gasps)

243
00:12:03,157 --> 00:12:05,407
Why isn't this thing vanishing?

244
00:12:05,490 --> 00:12:06,033
Is it still alive?

245
00:12:06,115 --> 00:12:08,074
(gasps) No!

246
00:12:08,157 --> 00:12:10,077
It's not a cursed spirit,
it has a physical body!

247
00:12:11,115 --> 00:12:14,866
-(horn blares)
-(Kugisaki gasps)

248
00:12:14,949 --> 00:12:16,824
Watch your ass!

249
00:12:16,907 --> 00:12:17,907
Christ.

250
00:12:18,866 --> 00:12:21,033
(passenger yelps)

251
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:21,866
(driver gasps) Sawamura?

252
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,866
Speed up.

253
00:12:24,949 --> 00:12:26,949
Hit the brakes and you're dead.

254
00:12:27,033 --> 00:12:29,490
Both you and him, you got that?

255
00:12:32,533 --> 00:12:35,241
(tires squealing)

256
00:12:36,992 --> 00:12:38,134
-(passenger whimpering)
-(blood squelches)

257
00:12:38,158 --> 00:12:39,491
(passenger screams)

258
00:12:39,575 --> 00:12:41,992
Listen, you, don't follow me.

259
00:12:42,075 --> 00:12:43,616
Once I'm healed,

260
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:47,283
I'll make sure to kill these
two, especially that woman.

261
00:12:47,366 --> 00:12:47,950
I'm sorry, Kechizu.

262
00:12:48,034 --> 00:12:51,116
I wasn't able to mourn you

263
00:12:51,199 --> 00:12:54,908
but I promise you, I
will get revenge for...

264
00:12:54,992 --> 00:12:57,450
What the hell?
What is she doing?

265
00:12:57,533 --> 00:12:57,950
Kugisaki!

266
00:12:58,034 --> 00:12:59,075
(Straw Doll swishes)

267
00:12:59,158 --> 00:13:01,450
(nail clangs) (blue
light swooshes)

268
00:13:01,533 --> 00:13:04,617
Yeah, don't rush me, okay?

269
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:06,242
Straw Doll Technique!

270
00:13:08,076 --> 00:13:09,743
Resonance!

271
00:13:09,826 --> 00:13:13,159
-(blue light swooshes)
-(weapon clangs)

272
00:13:13,242 --> 00:13:15,159
(blood sloshes)

273
00:13:15,242 --> 00:13:17,576
(Eso gasps)

274
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:22,492
[Narrator] Once sorcerers
land a Black Flash,

275
00:13:22,576 --> 00:13:23,951
they temporarily enter a state

276
00:13:24,035 --> 00:13:26,284
that athletes
commonly call the zone.

277
00:13:27,117 --> 00:13:29,076
(Itadori thuds)

278
00:13:29,159 --> 00:13:32,036
That hurts. (yells)

279
00:13:32,118 --> 00:13:35,077
So it wasn't a technique
to turn the curse of the user.

280
00:13:37,577 --> 00:13:39,160
(blue light sizzles)

281
00:13:39,243 --> 00:13:40,243
Sorry.

282
00:13:40,327 --> 00:13:43,952
(blue light swooshes)

283
00:13:44,036 --> 00:13:45,952
(Itadori thuds)

284
00:13:46,036 --> 00:13:49,785
(energy thundering)

285
00:13:49,869 --> 00:13:52,327
(somber music)

286
00:13:53,994 --> 00:13:57,410
(smoke hisses)

287
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,619
That hurt.

288
00:14:03,786 --> 00:14:06,703
(game clicking)

289
00:14:06,786 --> 00:14:08,745
All right, Geto, pay up.

290
00:14:08,828 --> 00:14:09,037
What's the matter, Choso?

291
00:14:09,119 --> 00:14:11,536
Come on.

292
00:14:11,619 --> 00:14:12,828
(object cracks)

293
00:14:12,911 --> 00:14:14,995
Whoa, hey, what'd
you do that for?

294
00:14:15,078 --> 00:14:17,369
Both of my bothers just died.

295
00:14:17,453 --> 00:14:19,578
You can sense that from here?

296
00:14:19,661 --> 00:14:20,536
[Choso] What's going on?

297
00:14:20,619 --> 00:14:22,220
It'd be one thing if he
was fully manifested,

298
00:14:22,244 --> 00:14:25,078
but I can't believe both
my brothers were killed

299
00:14:25,161 --> 00:14:27,328
by a single finger
of a cursed spirit.

300
00:14:27,411 --> 00:14:28,536
Just a minute.

301
00:14:28,619 --> 00:14:30,829
[Mahito] Crap, there
aren't any spares.

302
00:14:30,912 --> 00:14:32,704
Why did you have
to break that one?

303
00:14:32,787 --> 00:14:34,120
[Geto] I just got the report.

304
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:36,203
Eso and Kechizu were killed

305
00:14:36,287 --> 00:14:38,245
by first-years
from Jujutsu High.

306
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:42,579
Yuji Itadori and his group.

307
00:14:46,495 --> 00:14:49,370
(Mahito laughs)

308
00:14:49,454 --> 00:14:52,454
(blinkers clicking)

309
00:14:52,537 --> 00:14:55,079
[Voice Mail] The person you
have dialed is not responding.

310
00:14:55,162 --> 00:14:56,805
If you feel you have
reached this number in error-

311
00:14:56,829 --> 00:14:58,871
-Why don't they answer?
-(car revving)

312
00:14:58,954 --> 00:15:00,747
Where did those brats go?

313
00:15:03,039 --> 00:15:06,621
[Itadori] Kugisaki, you okay?

314
00:15:06,705 --> 00:15:08,246
Oh, I'm okay.

315
00:15:08,330 --> 00:15:09,955
I might have some
scarring, though.

316
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:11,872
I wonder if those two old dudes

317
00:15:11,955 --> 00:15:13,413
in the truck are all right?

318
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:15,872
And the poisons...

319
00:15:15,955 --> 00:15:19,080
Wow, I wonder if we head
home now if Shoko will be awake

320
00:15:19,163 --> 00:15:20,180
and if she'll still be sober?

321
00:15:20,204 --> 00:15:23,455
It's creeping me out
that you're being so quiet.

322
00:15:24,872 --> 00:15:27,080
[Itadori] I was wondering,
was this your first time

323
00:15:27,163 --> 00:15:29,246
killing instead of exorcizing?

324
00:15:29,330 --> 00:15:31,622
Mm-hmm. What about you?

325
00:15:31,706 --> 00:15:33,181
Yeah, I did have to
do it one other time.

326
00:15:33,205 --> 00:15:36,164
No, I guess it's
wrong to call it one.

327
00:15:36,247 --> 00:15:37,372
There were three.

328
00:15:37,456 --> 00:15:39,622
Then I think you're doing
worse here than I am

329
00:15:39,706 --> 00:15:40,873
from the sound of it.

330
00:15:42,081 --> 00:15:44,414
What just happened
meant nothing to me.

331
00:15:44,497 --> 00:15:45,998
Just another day for a sorcerer.

332
00:15:46,081 --> 00:15:49,622
And, I'm no Fushiguro here,

333
00:15:49,706 --> 00:15:53,247
but ultimately there are only
so many people we can save.

334
00:15:53,331 --> 00:15:56,122
Like, if I think of my life
as a bus ride, you know,

335
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:59,665
I don't want to get my
heart swayed by someone

336
00:15:59,749 --> 00:16:02,498
who shouldn't have had
a seat in the first place.

337
00:16:02,582 --> 00:16:03,582
Too mean?

338
00:16:04,915 --> 00:16:07,123
But, then sometimes
there are people like you

339
00:16:07,206 --> 00:16:09,665
who bring their own seat
and just sit right down.

340
00:16:11,332 --> 00:16:14,332
If it helps, we didn't have
room back there to worry about

341
00:16:14,415 --> 00:16:17,123
whether they were cursed
spirits or curse users.

342
00:16:17,206 --> 00:16:19,665
Even if they were human,
we don't have a technique

343
00:16:19,749 --> 00:16:22,332
to keep anyone that
strong restrained long-term.

344
00:16:22,415 --> 00:16:23,957
You know that, right?

345
00:16:24,041 --> 00:16:27,957
Yeah, but, he was crying
watching his brother die.

346
00:16:30,207 --> 00:16:31,207
[Kugisaki] I see.

347
00:16:31,291 --> 00:16:33,499
[Itadori] Don't get me wrong.

348
00:16:33,583 --> 00:16:36,333
I'm happy you and I were
spared and we're still alive.

349
00:16:36,416 --> 00:16:38,207
It's a big relief.

350
00:16:38,291 --> 00:16:41,166
But, the fact remains
tears were shed

351
00:16:41,249 --> 00:16:43,583
over the lives I ended tonight.

352
00:16:44,583 --> 00:16:45,583
That's all.

353
00:16:46,291 --> 00:16:47,291
[Kugisaki] I see.

354
00:16:48,416 --> 00:16:52,000
In that case, you
and I are accomplices.

355
00:16:54,416 --> 00:16:56,374
[Both] (gasp) Fushiguro?

356
00:16:57,583 --> 00:17:00,334
(moans) Oh, you're back.

357
00:17:00,417 --> 00:17:01,876
Glad you're safe.

358
00:17:01,959 --> 00:17:03,876
[Both] Yay, I was scared!

359
00:17:03,959 --> 00:17:07,375
I thought you were
dead for sure, thank god!

360
00:17:07,459 --> 00:17:09,876
Could you lower
your voices please?

361
00:17:09,959 --> 00:17:11,542
My head hurts.

362
00:17:11,625 --> 00:17:13,375
Don't go to sleep
holding Sukuna's finger.

363
00:17:13,459 --> 00:17:15,084
That thing's dangerous.

364
00:17:15,167 --> 00:17:18,084
And how would you
know about the finger?

365
00:17:18,167 --> 00:17:20,334
[Kugisaki] You have the
energy to ask about that?

366
00:17:20,417 --> 00:17:22,625
Nope, let's go ahead
and contact Nitta.

367
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:25,834
We need to seal this
from cursed spirits.

368
00:17:25,917 --> 00:17:27,375
They're coming for it.

369
00:17:27,459 --> 00:17:29,460
Oh wait, should I eat it?

370
00:17:29,543 --> 00:17:31,102
[Kugisaki] It's not
some midnight snack!

371
00:17:31,126 --> 00:17:31,918
We don't have a clear idea

372
00:17:32,002 --> 00:17:33,960
of how many fingers
you can handle.

373
00:17:34,044 --> 00:17:35,585
So, don't eat it.

374
00:17:35,668 --> 00:17:39,209
But I will hand it over to you
since you have the most energy.

375
00:17:39,293 --> 00:17:43,251
I'll say it once more
though, do not eat this.

376
00:17:45,293 --> 00:17:47,835
(mouth gulps)

377
00:17:49,044 --> 00:17:50,044
Huh?

378
00:17:51,209 --> 00:17:53,752
(grunts) He thinks I have
the intelligence of a dog!

379
00:17:53,835 --> 00:17:55,102
-I said don't eat it!
-He said don't eat it!

380
00:17:55,126 --> 00:17:56,209
Huh? What?

381
00:17:56,293 --> 00:17:58,419
I'm not the one
who ate it, he is!

382
00:17:58,502 --> 00:18:00,753
Sukuna didn't even
warn me this time either.

383
00:18:02,003 --> 00:18:02,586
[Gojo] The Sukuna within you

384
00:18:02,669 --> 00:18:04,794
will try to regain his power

385
00:18:04,878 --> 00:18:07,461
and that will lead
us to the fingers.

386
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:10,086
Has Gojo just been
winging it this whole time?

387
00:18:10,169 --> 00:18:11,586
[Fushiguro] You
just realized that?

388
00:18:11,669 --> 00:18:14,086
There you are, you
three little jerks!

389
00:18:14,169 --> 00:18:15,961
What have you been
doing all this time?

390
00:18:16,045 --> 00:18:16,961
[Itadori] Oh, it's Nitta.

391
00:18:17,045 --> 00:18:18,478
[Kugisaki] And it
sounds like she's lost it.

392
00:18:18,502 --> 00:18:20,461
[Nitta] I called! What's
the big idea, huh?

393
00:18:20,544 --> 00:18:22,586
-All right, let's go.
-(Nitta yelling)

394
00:18:22,669 --> 00:18:24,395
[Nitta] Keep things from
going sideways and you three-

395
00:18:24,419 --> 00:18:25,895
-[Kugisaki] I'm hungry.
-(Nitta yelling)

396
00:18:25,919 --> 00:18:27,229
I wonder if there's a
Splendid Sushi around here.

397
00:18:27,253 --> 00:18:29,628
[Itadori] Splendid
Sushi's bullet train

398
00:18:29,712 --> 00:18:30,754
was awesome, wasn't it?

399
00:18:30,837 --> 00:18:31,837
[Kugisaki] Shut up.

400
00:18:32,253 --> 00:18:34,253
Turns out it wasn't

401
00:18:34,337 --> 00:18:35,354
just a cursed
spirit with a finger.

402
00:18:35,378 --> 00:18:38,628
When we analyzed the
corpses, what a surprise.

403
00:18:38,712 --> 00:18:41,004
It was the manifestation
of the other goods

404
00:18:42,545 --> 00:18:45,087
and each of them took
out one special-grade.

405
00:18:45,170 --> 00:18:47,670
And this year's first-years
are the cream of the crop.

406
00:18:47,754 --> 00:18:50,503
I guess it's my amazing
skill as an instructor.

407
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:53,128
[Utahime] I don't want
any long chats with you

408
00:18:53,211 --> 00:18:53,920
on my day off.

409
00:18:54,004 --> 00:18:55,378
You're calling
about arrangements

410
00:18:55,462 --> 00:18:57,129
for the drinking party, right?

411
00:18:57,212 --> 00:18:58,671
[Gojo] Well, find
any candidates?

412
00:18:58,755 --> 00:19:00,005
No, none.

413
00:19:00,088 --> 00:19:01,397
Everyone's busy,
including myself.

414
00:19:01,421 --> 00:19:05,005
What now? Should I
try inviting the students?

415
00:19:05,088 --> 00:19:06,838
Sure, I'm a lightweight,
so I don't mind

416
00:19:06,921 --> 00:19:08,671
if the party's alcohol-free.

417
00:19:08,755 --> 00:19:09,671
You can do it.

418
00:19:09,755 --> 00:19:10,880
Keep asking around.

419
00:19:14,088 --> 00:19:16,171
(Gojo sighs)

420
00:19:16,254 --> 00:19:17,838
You never know what
might be listening

421
00:19:17,921 --> 00:19:20,296
around Utahime, after all.

422
00:19:20,379 --> 00:19:21,838
I don't want to think about

423
00:19:21,921 --> 00:19:23,504
one of the students
being the traitor.

424
00:19:24,504 --> 00:19:25,504
This is such a pain.

425
00:19:27,589 --> 00:19:29,964
Well, leave the
rest of you, Mei Mei.

426
00:19:32,130 --> 00:19:34,505
(mellow music)

427
00:19:37,630 --> 00:19:39,756
(Mei Mei laughing)

428
00:19:39,839 --> 00:19:41,172
[Fushiguro] Don't
talk about them

429
00:19:41,255 --> 00:19:42,255
resonating with Itadori.

430
00:19:42,339 --> 00:19:44,255
[Kugisaki] Are you
certain about that?

431
00:19:44,339 --> 00:19:45,380
I think so.

432
00:19:45,464 --> 00:19:47,505
The case is over, though.

433
00:19:47,589 --> 00:19:51,881
The only ones likely to
notice would be us and Nitta.

434
00:19:54,297 --> 00:19:57,214
Itadori and Sukuna's
manifestation

435
00:19:57,298 --> 00:19:58,298
was only the trigger.

436
00:19:58,798 --> 00:20:00,715
The curse of Yasohachi
Bridge could've started

437
00:20:00,798 --> 00:20:01,715
killing at any moment.

438
00:20:01,798 --> 00:20:05,049
Besides, when he
swallowed that first finger

439
00:20:05,131 --> 00:20:06,381
it was to save me.

440
00:20:06,465 --> 00:20:10,590
But, there's no way he'd
be satisfied with just that.

441
00:20:10,673 --> 00:20:12,465
So, don't tell him.

442
00:20:12,548 --> 00:20:14,090
I won't say anything.

443
00:20:14,173 --> 00:20:15,506
Girls know how to be discreet.

444
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:18,465
This is all your fault.

445
00:20:18,548 --> 00:20:19,631
You took me in.

446
00:20:19,715 --> 00:20:24,214
And now the severed parts
of my soul have all awakened.

447
00:20:24,298 --> 00:20:27,299
(laughs) In order to save
lots of people, was it?

448
00:20:27,382 --> 00:20:29,382
You little punk.

449
00:20:29,466 --> 00:20:31,424
Other people are gonna
die because you live.

450
00:20:31,507 --> 00:20:34,507
[Itadori] Hey, don't
say that to Fushiguro.

451
00:20:35,174 --> 00:20:37,382
How are you going to feel
when someone you save

452
00:20:37,466 --> 00:20:38,826
goes on to kill
someone else later?

453
00:20:40,632 --> 00:20:43,591
[Itadori] Don't you dare say it.

454
00:20:43,674 --> 00:20:46,424
(Zen'in grunting)

455
00:20:49,382 --> 00:20:50,591
(Panda grunts)

456
00:20:50,674 --> 00:20:51,382
(Maki gasps)

457
00:20:51,466 --> 00:20:53,966
(punch thuds)

458
00:20:54,050 --> 00:20:54,592
(Panda laughs)

459
00:20:54,675 --> 00:20:57,133
[Toge] Mustard leaf.

460
00:20:57,216 --> 00:20:58,484
Your reactions don't
seem very sharp today.

461
00:20:58,508 --> 00:21:00,759
What's the deal?

462
00:21:00,842 --> 00:21:02,216
Shut up.

463
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:04,759
All that time off
cost me my edge.

464
00:21:04,842 --> 00:21:06,425
Yeah, obviously.

465
00:21:06,508 --> 00:21:08,592
So, did you hear
about the first-years?

466
00:21:08,675 --> 00:21:12,133
Yeah, I heard they took
out three special-grades.

467
00:21:12,216 --> 00:21:12,592
Is that true?

468
00:21:12,675 --> 00:21:13,675
[Toge] Salmon.

469
00:21:15,425 --> 00:21:19,383
Well, in that case, we
don't want to fall behind.

470
00:21:19,467 --> 00:21:20,717
So, let's get to it.

471
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:21,467
[Toge] Roe.

472
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:25,259
Yeah! (gasps)

473
00:21:26,593 --> 00:21:27,509
(Maki grunts)

474
00:21:27,593 --> 00:21:29,760
[Panda] Hey, you hit
me for real that time!

475
00:21:29,843 --> 00:21:30,634
[Maki] It wouldn't
be good training

476
00:21:30,718 --> 00:21:31,634
if I wasn't serious, would it?

477
00:21:31,718 --> 00:21:32,843
[Toge] Kelp.

478
00:21:32,926 --> 00:21:35,593
Even among sorcerers,
the rank of special-grade

479
00:21:35,676 --> 00:21:39,010
is a position beyond
the normal scope.

480
00:21:39,093 --> 00:21:41,801
It's my conviction,
that it's the first-grades

481
00:21:41,885 --> 00:21:44,843
who should lead the other
sorcerers of the jujutsu world,

482
00:21:44,926 --> 00:21:47,843
given all the confidential
information and the danger.

483
00:21:47,926 --> 00:21:49,569
That, along with the pay
that they have to accept

484
00:21:49,593 --> 00:21:51,551
is nothing like what those

485
00:21:51,634 --> 00:21:54,177
semi-first-grade and
below must deal with.

486
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:56,802
So, with that in mind, what
are your recommendations?

487
00:21:56,886 --> 00:21:58,635
Maki Zen'in, Panda.

488
00:21:58,719 --> 00:22:01,469
Megumi Fushiguro
and Nobara Kugisaki

489
00:22:01,552 --> 00:22:05,635
and then, my
brother Yuji Itadori.

490
00:22:05,719 --> 00:22:09,177
So by my name, Aoi Todou...

491
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:11,469
[Mei Mei] And
by mine, Mei Mei...

492
00:22:11,552 --> 00:22:12,570
[Aoi Todou and Mei Mei] We
hereby recommend these five

493
00:22:12,594 --> 00:22:15,302
for promotion to first-grade.

494
00:22:18,635 --> 00:22:20,677
(Itadori moaning)

495
00:22:20,761 --> 00:22:24,345
[Itadori] I just think you're
buying way too much stuff.

496
00:22:24,428 --> 00:22:26,219
[Kugisaki] Half of
that is yours, isn't it?

497
00:22:26,303 --> 00:22:27,219
Huh? No.

498
00:22:27,303 --> 00:22:28,595
Only one is mine.

499
00:22:28,678 --> 00:22:30,595
-(Itadori grunts)
-(paper bag rustling)

500
00:22:30,678 --> 00:22:32,219
(Itadori sighs)

501
00:22:32,303 --> 00:22:33,345
Huh?

502
00:22:33,428 --> 00:22:36,511
You drop even one of
those bags and I'll kill you.

503
00:22:36,595 --> 00:22:37,595
Oh, right.

504
00:22:42,511 --> 00:22:44,887
(punch thuds)

505
00:22:44,970 --> 00:22:46,720
(Itadori grunts)

506
00:22:46,803 --> 00:22:49,678
I just told you that if you
drop even one you're dead!

507
00:22:49,762 --> 00:22:51,219
I'm sorry, it was an accident!

508
00:22:51,303 --> 00:22:52,905
-(Kugisaki growls)
-You just have too many bags!

509
00:22:52,929 --> 00:22:54,512
If any of my stuff gets damaged,

510
00:22:54,596 --> 00:22:56,155
-you're going to pay for it!
-(phone buzzing)

511
00:22:56,179 --> 00:22:57,096
Fushiguro.

512
00:22:57,179 --> 00:22:58,763
-(Itadori and
Kugisaki yelling) -Yes.

513
00:22:58,846 --> 00:22:59,929
Yeah.

514
00:23:00,013 --> 00:23:01,471
All right, see ya.

515
00:23:02,679 --> 00:23:05,096
What?

516
00:23:05,179 --> 00:23:07,679
Gojo says to
come in, it's urgent.

517
00:23:07,763 --> 00:23:08,637
[Itadori] Huh?

518
00:23:08,721 --> 00:23:09,929
[Kugisaki] Yeah? What for?

519
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:11,387
An assignment.

520
00:23:11,471 --> 00:23:13,262
He said it was top secret.

521
00:23:13,346 --> 00:23:14,697
[Kugisaki] Huh?
But we just finished

522
00:23:14,721 --> 00:23:16,387
doing a big mission for him.

523
00:23:16,471 --> 00:23:18,096
Sounds good to me.

524
00:23:18,179 --> 00:23:21,721
If Gojo's telling us it's
top secret, it must be big.

525
00:23:21,804 --> 00:23:23,597
He says that a lot.

526
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:25,597
Only every time.

527
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,889
Yeah, but so what?

528
00:23:31,472 --> 00:23:32,722
Let's go.

529
00:23:32,805 --> 00:23:35,305
(rock music)

